For a partial map $\phi \colon \G ightharpoonup k$ with finite domain, let $V_\phi \subseteq k^\G$ denote the clopen set given by \[ V_\phi \,\defeq\, \set{x \in k^\G \,:\, x \supset \phi}. \] Since the topology on $k^\G$ is generated by the sets of the form $V_\phi$, it is enough to prove Theorem~ef{theo:synd} with $V = V_\phi$. So, let $D \subset \G$ be a nonempty finite set and let $\phi \colon D 	o k$. Let $\ell_0 \in \N$ be such that  egin{equation} e \cdot (1 - k^{-|D|})^\ell \cdot |D|^2\ell^2 \,<\, 1 \qquad 	ext{for all } \ell \geq \ell_0. \end{equation} \ep{Such $\ell_0$ exists since the left-hand side of \eqref{eq:endgame} approaches $0$ as $\ell$ goes to infinity.} We shall argue that $n \defeq \ell_0|D|^2$ is as desired. Take any finite set $F \subset \G$ of size at least $n$ and let $L \subseteq F$ be a set of size at least $|F|/|D|^2 \geq \ell_0$ such that $L^{-1}$ is left $D$-separated \ep{such $L$ exists due to Lemma~ef{lemma:indep} applied with $F^{-1}$ in place of $F$}. Define a $k$-instance $\B$ over $\G$ as follows. For each $\gamma \in \G$, let $B_\gamma$ be the bad $k$-event with domain $D_\gamma \defeq D L^{-1}\gamma$ consisting of all maps $\psi \colon D_\gamma 	o k$ such that: \[ 	ext{for each } \lambda \in L,\ 	ext{there is } \delta \in D\ 	ext{with } \psi(\delta\lambda^{-1}\gamma) \,
eq\, \phi(\delta). \] Notice that since $L^{-1}$ is left $D$-separated, $D_\gamma$ is equal to the \emph{disjoint} union of the sets $D \lambda^{-1}\gamma$, $\lambda \in L$. Let $\B\defeq \set{B_\gamma \,:\, \gamma \in \G}$. We claim that if $x \colon \G	o k$ is a solution to $\B$, then $x$ is trapped in $L \cdot V_\phi$ \ep{and hence also in $F \cdot V_\phi$}. Indeed, consider any $\gamma \in \G$. Since $x$ avoids $B_\gamma$, the following holds: \[ 	ext{there is } \lambda \in L\ 	ext{such that for all } \delta \in D, \ x(\delta \lambda^{-1}\gamma) \,=\, \phi(\delta). \] But this precisely means that for some $\lambda \in L$, $\lambda^{-1}\gamma \cdot x \supset \phi$, i.e., $\gamma \cdot x \in L \cdot V_\phi$. In view of Theorem~ef{theo:LLL}, it only remains to show that $\B$ is correct for the LLL. First we bound $d(\B)$. Consider any $\gamma \in \G$. We need to find an upper bound on the size of the set \[ \set{\gamma' \in \G \setminus \set{\gamma} \,:\, D_\gamma \cap D_{\gamma'} 
eq \0}. \] To this end, notice that $D_\gamma \cap D_{\gamma'} 
eq \0$ if and only if $\gamma' \in LD^{-1}DL^{-1}\gamma$. Thus, \[ \left|\set{\gamma' \in \G \setminus \set{\gamma} \,:\, D_\gamma \cap D_{\gamma'} 
eq \0}ight| \,=\, |LD^{-1}DL^{-1}| - 1 \,\leq\, |D|^2|L|^2 - 1, \] and hence we conclude that $d(\B) \leq |D|^2|L|^2 - 1$. Next we bound $p(\B)$. Again, fix $\gamma \in \G$ and draw $f \colon D_\gamma 	o k$ uniformly at random. Then for each $\lambda \in L$, \[ \P[f(\delta \lambda^{-1} \gamma) 
eq \phi(\delta) 	ext{ for some } \delta \in D] \,=\, 1 - k^{-|D|}, \] and since the sets $D \lambda^{-1}\gamma$, $\lambda \in L$ are disjoint, we conclude that \[ \P[B_\gamma] \,=\, (1 - k^{-|D|})^{|L|}. \] Therefore, $p(\B) \leq (1 - k^{-|D|})^{|L|}$. To put everything together, $\B$ is correct as long as \[ e \cdot (1 - k^{-|D|})^{|L|} \cdot |D|^2|L|^2 \,<\, 1. \] Since $|L| \geq \ell_0$, \eqref{eq:endgame} gives the desired result.

